# Copy this file to .env. Nothing here is required to build or load the
# extension. There's no OAuth setup either — the content script runs on the
# RStudio host itself (Posit Cloud / RStudio Server / Posit Workbench), so
# the logged-in session is the only credential the write path needs (see
# EXECUTION.md).

# Optional. If set, every raw text a student submits (successful or not — no
# names, no session/user id, nothing else) is POSTed here, fire-and-forget.
# Leave unset to disable input logging entirely (the default for a fresh
# clone). See Ninebark-DesmosExtension's google-apps-script/README.md for a
# free, ready-made endpoint that appends each input as a row in a Google
# Sheet you own — the same endpoint works here too.
VITE_INPUT_LOG_URL=

# Optional. The Ninebark AI-relay Worker's base URL (no trailing slash) —
# see /Users/dylanwinning/Ninebark-AIRelay. This is for the BROWSER
# extension (extension/src/rstudio.ts) only — the RStudio Addin (the R
# package in ninebark-r/) has its own, separate NINEBARK_AI_RELAY_URL R
# environment variable (set via .Renviron or the shell, not this file),
# documented in ninebark-r/R/aiRelayClient.R, since its V8 bridge can't
# make the network call itself (see that file's header for why). Leave
# this one unset to disable the AI-fallback tier entirely on the browser
# side (the default for a fresh clone). Raw-code-tier output from either
# side always targets insertion into the Source/Ace editor, unexecuted —
# never auto-run.
VITE_AI_RELAY_URL=
